// Type checking for the configuration files at the frontend root.
//
// The fourth and last project over this package. tsconfig.json covers src,
// tsconfig.e2e.json covers tests/e2e, tsconfig.e2e-root.json covers e2e, and
// until this file existed the 17 files that AIM all of that compiled nowhere:
// 16 playwright*.config.ts and vite.config.ts. A spec tree under a gate and the
// configuration that points at it left ungated is half a gate.
//
// Nothing read them at all, which is stronger than "no type checking" and was
// measured rather than assumed: eslint.config.js ignores '*.config.ts' by name,
// alongside 'e2e/**', so neither of this package's two readers looked at these
// files. That is how a dead /// <reference types="vitest" /> could sit on line 1
// of vite.config.ts with the whole test configuration unchecked behind it.
//
// What this catches and what it does not, stated because the difference is easy
// to lose. It catches a misspelled option, an option that no longer exists, and
// a value of the wrong type - vite.config.ts turned out to hold two of those on
// the day this landed. It does NOT catch a wrong VALUE: a testDir that sweeps a
// whole directory instead of one spec, or a testIgnore whose glob is correct
// against the repository and wrong against the machine it runs on, are both
// well-typed strings and no compiler will ever object to them. Catching those
// needs a gate that resolves each config against the filesystem and asserts a
// non-zero collection. This is the shape of these files, not their meaning.
//
// A separate project chained onto typecheck:e2e with && rather than another
// entry in an existing include, for the reason recorded in tsconfig.e2e.json:
// the whole-program check over src already OOM'd at a 6 GB heap, runs at 9 GB
// now, and macOS skips it because 9 GB exceeds that runner's RAM. Merging
// programs costs memory, not time; these 17 files cost seconds. Nothing here
// imports from src (measured, not assumed), so the program stays at 17.
//
// It extends the base config and overrides no compiler option, on purpose.
// Exempting configuration from strictness would leave the same hole under a
// nicer name, and it would do it in the files that are written rarely and read
// even more rarely, which is where a silent hole survives longest.
//
// The exclude mirrors .gitignore line 69. playwright.video.config.ts is ignored
// but is a root-level *.ts, so a checkout that has one would pull it into this
// program off the disk - tsc reads the disk, not the index - and the same
// command would answer differently here and in CI. There was no such file when
// this was written, and no other ignored root-level .ts either; that was
// measured on 2026-08-30 rather than assumed, and it is written down so the
// next reader can tell "checked, none" from "never checked".
//
// The boundary. Before this, 25 tracked .ts/.tsx files in this package were
// outside every project. After it, 8: e2e-match/match-iter.spec.ts,
// e2e-match/match.spec.ts, playwright/property-dev-buyer-edit.spec.ts,
// playwright/property-dev-drawer-a11y.spec.ts, scripts/pwa-install.spec.ts,
// tests/pwa/manifest.test.ts, tests/pwa/service-worker.test.ts and
// tests/splash/splashI18n.test.ts.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["playwright.video.config.ts"]
}
